[Intro]
Midnight.
One light in the building.
I’ve been waiting for permission
from a room that isn’t listening.
[Verse 1]
Ten years hunched over a blinking line,
Coffee gone cold, trading sleep for time.
Built every joint, knew the weight of the frame,
Had my fingerprints buried where nobody came.
Then the screen lit up with a different reply,
Put a week of work right in front of my eyes.
First came the silence, then came the doubt:
If I don’t lay the bricks, do they count me out?
Pulled up the thing that I never could finish,
Watched it take shape, put my own hands in it.
Still had to choose what to keep, what to kill—
Now the distance was smaller between want and will.
[Pre-Chorus]
Upstairs, another meeting.
Down here, something breathing.
They’re still reviewing the plan—
I’ve got it running in my hands!
[Chorus]
WHO HOLDS THE KEYS?
WE BUILD THE DOORS!
An idea shouldn’t die
on a boardroom floor!
WHO HOLDS THE KEYS?
WHAT ARE WE WAITING FOR?
Got a world inside our heads—
LET IT OUT! LET IT ROAR!
[Verse 2]
Bought the machine, but the lock came free,
Fine print telling me what I’m allowed to be.
Pay for the tool, pay again for the right,
Watch another feature disappear overnight.
Six suits deep in a sign-off chain,
New slide deck with the same old pain.
“Circle back.” “Next quarter.” “Stay in your lane.”
There’s a kid downstairs making all that change.
Built for a friend with a need and no budget,
Left the source open so somebody could touch it.
Somebody fixed what I couldn’t get right,
Woke to a better version overnight.
[Pre-Chorus]
No badge on the table.
No seat with my name.
Just a thing that works
and a hand on the frame!
[Chorus]
WHO HOLDS THE KEYS?
WE BUILD THE DOORS!
An idea shouldn’t die
on a boardroom floor!
WHO HOLDS THE KEYS?
WHAT ARE WE WAITING FOR?
Got a world inside our heads—
LET IT OUT! LET IT ROAR!
[Bridge]
I still miss the quiet
of a problem solved by hand.
Still look beneath the surface.
Still need to understand.
But there’s a sketch beside the keyboard
that’s been waiting there for years.
Tonight I get to build it.
Tonight it leaves here.
[Breakdown]
Who decides what matters?
WE DO! WE DO!
Who checks what we’re making?
WE DO! WE DO!
A thousand lines a second—
But what are they for?
Put a purpose in the circuit!
Put your shoulder to the door!
[Final Chorus]
WHO HOLDS THE KEYS?
WE BUILD THE DOORS!
An idea shouldn’t die
on a boardroom floor!
WHO HOLDS THE KEYS?
WHAT ARE WE WAITING FOR?
Got a world inside our heads—
LET IT OUT! LET IT ROAR!
[Outro]
Midnight.
One light in the building.
Something new is running.
Someone else can build on it.
